<title>THAILAND: Alphatec Electronics sets up in Japan.</title>
<headline>Alphatec Electronics sets up in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alphatec Electronics Plc, one of Thailand's largest electronics companies, will establish a new Japanese subsidiary, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand, Alphatec said it would spend 10 million yen establishing a 100 percent-owned subsidiary, called Alphatec Japan Limited (Nippon Alphatec) in Minatoku, Tokyo.</p>
<p>The subsidiary will provide a base for expansion into the Asia-Pacific region and source raw materials for the parent company, the statement said.</p>
<p>(US$1 = 120 yen)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
